Janis Papanagnou wrote:
> Slarty wrote:
>
>> 2 Qs:1)Is there some way to tell whether an altar jives with you
>> before taking the risk of praying or sacraficing?
>
> A jiving altar??? No idea what you are talking about. Just guessing...

Co-aligned.

> 1. Stand on the altar and use command ':' to see whether its alignment
> matches yours; don't pray on non-coaligned altars.

I have not tried "/" far-see on an altar in years so I don't remember if
it also works.  There are reasons to pray on a cross-aligned altar in
extraordinary circumstances - You need to be able to describe those
circumstances before ever doing it.

> 2. Whether you are already admitted to pray or not is generally not
> easy (i.e. impossible) to calculate (see Wiki for details). Usually
> I wait a couple hundred turns before I pray again.

I name an item with the turn number of my prayer.

> 3. Use potions or wands of enlightenment to see whether you can pray.

Nice to have.

> 4. If you sacrifice on an altar; as long as you get "hopefully feelings"
> don't pray. It's save if you get "reconcilliation" or if the "hopefully
> feeling" messages stopped while sacrificing.

I don't see the risk is that big for sacrificing on a cross-aligned
altar unless it's a shrine with a resident priest.  Each XP level gained
increases the chance you'll convert the altar.  If you fail your luck is
decreased but your deity is not angered.  If you suceed the luck is
easily replaced.  By the time I'm XP=5 or higher I don't worry about
converting all of the altars in a game but one in the main dungeon until
the Castle.

>> 2)Is there any reason to pray at an altar, w/out sacraficing.
>
> I use that mostly only for water prayer; drop potions of water on the
> altar and pray to get them changed to holy water. (I only pray if I am
> in trouble, e.g. if I am very low on HP's or weak from hunger.)

There are a lot of extra benefits that can be given by prayer at an
altar.  Especially once you have built up your luck you can get unthing
from extra problems solved to getting crowned.  At other squares you
might pray while Weak to prevent starvation.  At an altar you might pray
to get your helmet uncursed.  Even better, at an altar you can make
offerings and know for certain if you are safe to pray.


